# A search result shows the line it matched on, with the words lit — and that
# highlighting stays out of find's count.
#
# THIS SCRIPT USED TO PROVE NEITHER. It typed "workers" and asserted the
# snippet "1 of 3 workers has reported", which is session r6's PREVIEW; the row
# matched on its TITLE, which also says "workers", and r6 is not in the
# in-memory LRU — so snippet_for's transcript branch, the feature the commit
# sells, never ran. Deleting that branch left the test green. docs/SEARCH.md
# S10.
#
# The query is "before" now. It is in exactly one title in the catalog (t2's
# "needs a decision before it can go on") and t2 is the restored tab, so its
# transcript IS held — and the word is in the first message, not in the
# preview. So the line asserted below can only come from the transcript, and
# falling back to the preview ("two accounts do not reconcile") fails.
#
# [APP-WORKAROUND] Painting behind a run of text means knowing where that run
# landed on screen, and nothing in the library will say (afterhours_gaps.md
# #51). The band positions are re-derived by redoing the renderer's own layout,
# the same trick src/ui/find_highlight.h uses — and now literally the same
# code, so there is one transcription of the renderer's constants rather than
# two that rot apart.
#
# The counters, though, are two, and this script is why. find's band count is
# what corroborates find's tally (find_counts_only_what_it_could_paint.e2e). A
# band painted in the SIDEBAR is not one of those, so it is counted separately:
# here both audits are on at once, the sidebar paints one band and find still
# reports exactly its two.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_FIND_DEMO=delta HANABI_FIND_AUDIT=1 HANABI_SNIPPET_AUDIT=1

# The find query is "delta" and not "ledger" for one reason: expect_text is a
# substring match over every visible label, and with three "ledger" matches the
# tally "1 of 3" would also be satisfied by a sidebar row. "delta" matches the
# two account lines and nothing else.
#
# Before the sidebar is searched at all: find's tally and find's bands agree.
expect_text "1 of 2"
expect_text "bands 2"

# Search the list. The row that matches now carries the line it matched on —
# out of the conversation, not out of the preview.
click 140 58
wait_frames 4
type "before"
wait_frames 10
# The row's own title, cut short: a sidebar row ellipsizes what does not fit,
# so the assertion stops before the end of it.
expect_text "needs a decision before it"
# The preview, which is what the row falls back to when the transcript branch
# does not run, is "two accounts do not reconcile" — a different line.
expect_text "…against the ledger before the batch runs."

# One occurrence in that snippet, one band painted behind it.
expect_text "snippet bands 1"

# And find's own numbers are untouched by it — same tally, same bands.
expect_text "1 of 2"
expect_text "bands 2"
